thers:3","kind":"choice","options":["It had the best wind conditions","It was near their home","It had a big airport","It was in the mountains"],"q":"Why did they test their ideas at Kitty Hawk?"},{"id":"library:wright-brothers:4","kind":"open","max":100,"min":20,"q":"The brothers learned from bicycles, kites and a toy helicopter. How can playing with simple things help people invent big things?"},{"id":"library:wright-brothers:5","kind":"open","max":100,"min":20,"q":"Before 1903, most people thought flying machines were impossible. What seems impossible today but may be possible in the future?"}],"source":{"license":"public domain","name":"VOA Learning English (Marilyn Rice Christiano, adapted by John Russell)","note":"the broadcast sign-off removed","url":"https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/wilbur-and-orville-wright-the-first-airplane/7998765.html"},"subtitle":"Two brothers who liked bicycles and kites built the first plane with an engine.","title":"Wilbur and Orville Wright: The First Airplane","topic":"history","words":443}
